::MCR_U05_L03_GuidedPractice_Q01::
Question ID: MCR_U05_L03_GP_Q01
MLA Standard: MLA.MCR.PR.4
Question:
A number cube is rolled. What is the probability of rolling a 1 or a 2?
{
=A. 2/6#Correct. The outcomes 1 and 2 are two favorable outcomes out of six total.
~B. 1/6#This counts only one outcome. The word or includes both 1 and 2.
~C. 2/12#This incorrectly multiplies. An or question uses addition or counting the union.
~D. 4/6#This counts too many outcomes. Only 1 and 2 are favorable.
}
::MCR_U05_L03_GuidedPractice_Q02::
Question ID: MCR_U05_L03_GP_Q02
MLA Standard: MLA.MCR.PR.4
Question:
A number cube is rolled. What is the probability of rolling an even number or a number greater than 4?
{
~A. 5/6#This counts 6 twice. The overlap must be subtracted or listed once.
=B. 4/6#Correct. The union is \{2, 4, 5, 6\}, which is 4 outcomes out of 6.
~C. 1/6#This is only the overlap, not the full union.
~D. 3/6#This counts only the even outcomes and leaves out 5.
}
::MCR_U05_L03_GuidedPractice_Q03::
Question ID: MCR_U05_L03_GP_Q03
MLA Standard: MLA.MCR.PR.5
Question:
A coin is flipped and a number cube is rolled. What is the probability of heads and rolling a 6?
{
~A. 2/8#This adds counts from two different sample spaces. Independent and means multiply probabilities.
~B. 1/6#This only uses the number cube event and ignores the coin.
=C. 1/12#Correct. Multiply 1/2 by 1/6 to get 1/12.
~D. 7/12#This adds probabilities instead of multiplying for both events happening.
}
::MCR_U05_L03_GuidedPractice_Q04::
Question ID: MCR_U05_L03_GP_Q04
MLA Standard: MLA.MCR.PR.5
Question:
Two fair coins are flipped. What is the probability of getting heads on both coins?
{
~A. 1/2#This is the probability for one coin only. Two coins require both events.
~B. 2/2#This assumes both outcomes must happen, but probability must compare favorable outcomes to all outcomes.
~C. 2/4#This counts outcomes with at least one head, not both heads.
=D. 1/4#Correct. The outcomes are HH, HT, TH, TT, and only HH has heads on both coins.
}
::MCR_U05_L03_GuidedPractice_Q05::
Question ID: MCR_U05_L03_GP_Q05
MLA Standard: MLA.MCR.PR.4
Question:
A number cube is rolled. What is the probability of rolling an odd number or a 6?
{
~A. 3/6#This counts only odd outcomes and leaves out 6.
=B. 4/6#Correct. The favorable outcomes are \{1, 3, 5, 6\}, or 4 out of 6.
~C. 1/6#This counts only rolling a 6.
~D. 3/12#This incorrectly multiplies for an or question.
}
